WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.010
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.120
happening all the time,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.190
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.540
to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.490
This is the KimChi Chic Beauty

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.340
Pearl Gone Wild pressed
shimmer highlighter.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.010
This highlighter is so
stunning in the pan.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.376
It's like this iridescent pearl color

00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:17.884
that shifts to blue.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.290
There's a lot of glitter in this,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.990
which can look chunky or
make your skin look textured,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.030
but this actually went on beautifully.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.490
The glow it gives is unreal,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.160
and that blue sparkle adds
a little something special.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.630
It's not going to be for everyone,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.190
especially if you hate glitter,

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.890
but this formula is so pretty,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.790
and I really want more colors.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.727
Patrick Ta released these Major Skin

00:00:37.727 --> 00:00:40.140
crème foundation and
finishing powder duos.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.598
I love the packaging on this,

00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:43.006
especially this little flap

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:44.970
to protect the foundation from the powder.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.845
I went in with my foundation brush first,

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:48.978
and, wow, this is full coverage,

00:00:48.978 --> 00:00:50.250
and a little goes a long way.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.820
I did my entire face with
just one dip into the pan.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.610
I went over that with a sponge
to pick up excess product.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.130
I wouldn't say the finish
is super skin-like.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.810
It definitely looks and feels

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.370
like you're wearing foundation.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.900
But for something this full coverage,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.400
it doesn't look cakey to me.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.950
It's also a more dewy
finish, which I think helps.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.240
These are the Uoma Beauty

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.060
Black Magic Hypnotic Impact
high-shine lipsticks.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.030
I am so into shiny lipstick
formulas these days.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.640
Formula aside though, these
lipsticks are gorgeous.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.050
The embossing, the glitter,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.150
I could not stop staring at them.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.950
They look just as beautiful on the lips.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.100
This formula is literally a
lip gloss in lipstick form,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.166
so you get the shine

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:29.291
and you get that moisturizing feeling.

00:01:29.291 --> 00:01:30.720
The glitter is an overspray,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.436
so they don't look glittery on the lips,

00:01:32.436 --> 00:01:33.602
but I love these.

00:01:33.602 --> 00:01:35.250
This is the Merit Bronze Balm,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.770
and it's supposedly the
"easiest bronzer ever."

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.595
It's definitely the easiest bronzer

00:01:39.595 --> 00:01:41.161
I think I've ever used.

00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:43.560
It takes little to no
effort to blend this out,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.947
and it didn't break up the
product I already had on.

00:01:45.947 --> 00:01:47.850
I was worried the shade
I got was too light,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.770
but I think it actually turned out OK.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.130
It is buildable, I just wish
the color wasn't so sheer.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.930
Other than that, I like this.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.878
I'm seeing transfer-proof bullet lipsticks

00:01:56.878 --> 00:01:58.436
pop up a lot more lately.

00:01:58.436 --> 00:02:00.936
This one is the Nars Powermatte lipstick.

00:02:00.936 --> 00:02:03.120
It has a really amazing color payoff.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.640
This can definitely be
a one-swipe lipstick.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.530
The texture is so unique.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.853
The best way I can describe it is that it

00:02:09.853 --> 00:02:12.750
kind of feels like the
Nars soft matte packaging

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.180
on its products, but on your lips.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.210
It's this soft, powdery,
comfortable kind of matte

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.950
that felt really nice on the lips,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.800
and it is transfer-proof,
so I highly recommend this.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.530
This is the REM Beauty
Space Shape brow gel.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.488
What really drew me in to this product

00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:28.654
was the applicator.

00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:30.570
I've never seen one like this before,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.550
with a little doe foot on one side

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.990
and a comb on the other.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.383
It was really easy to use,

00:02:35.383 --> 00:02:37.500
and I like how it distributed the product.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.166
The actual brow gel is nice.

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:40.324
It did what it had to do,

00:02:40.324 --> 00:02:42.360
and it didn't leave my
brows feeling crunchy.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.310
As much as I like the applicator, though,

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.100
I don't feel like the
formula is anything special.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.310
KVD has reformulated its
iconic liquid lipstick,

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.260
so I picked up a few shades to try.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.280
Just like everybody else,

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.040
I was very big into the
shade Lolita back in the day,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.580
so I had to get Queen of
Poisons, which is its new name.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.638
I'm gonna be honest.

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:02.337
I can't really tell much of a difference

00:03:02.337 --> 00:03:04.530
between this formula and the old one.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.840
I think it maybe feels a
little more lightweight,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.250
but it still feels like I'm wearing

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.290
a slightly drying liquid lipstick.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.850
I do really like the colors I got,

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.980
but this bright orange was pretty patchy.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.802
I actually remember
having the same problem

00:03:15.802 --> 00:03:18.063
with the brighter colors
in the old formula too,

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:19.080
so that's not great.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.880
I also don't like this new packaging.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.500
The wand is so weirdly long.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.730
I don't know if you can tell,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.100
but it was kind of hard to
control when I was applying.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.810
I have been dying to try these Versed

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.660
Mood Lighting Luminizing
Glow Drops for a while.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.150
People say that this is
another Flawless Filter dupe.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.640
It does give a really
beautiful glow to the skin,

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.560
but there's not really any coverage to it,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.960
so I wouldn't call this a dupe exactly.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.290
It's like Flawless Filter's
more natural little sister.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.450
It has a lot of great skincare ingredients

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.000
that made my skin feel
really nice and hydrated.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.400
I actually preferred the
drops under my foundation

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.850
rather than on their own,
but I like these a lot.

